From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:21:41 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] arcade-carts

Each arcade board gets its own shelf object in the retro bitmap renderer
(ADR 0054), drawn face-on like every other shell. Neo Geo is the AES home
cart, 190 x 140 mm (seated 240x177, drawn 360x266), in black: the
recessed label well at the top edge, the centre seam and the two bands
of eight ribs above the connector end. The MVS arcade cart carries its
game only on a narrow top-edge strip, so it cannot show a game's art on
a face-on shelf. CPS2 is the B-board top cover, standing (seated
162x240, drawn 222x329): chamfered top corners, the screw, the white
serial sticker, two slanted vent grilles and the moulded CAPCOM, in the
colour of the set's region from its title (Japan green, Asia grey,
Hispanic and Brazil orange, rental yellow, else blue). CPS1 is the grey
CPS Changer and CPS 1.5 case seen from above (seated 240x200, drawn
360x300): the raised plinth that carries the label, the speaker grille,
the serial sticker, the front bosses and the moulded CAPCOM.

Label art is shown whole inside the well, centred on its own edge
colour, as the Master System box is: an arcade set's art is usually a
portrait flyer. A shell colour chosen in Config/cart_shell.txt still
wins. The outlines and reliefs are ours (neogeo_cart*.svg, cps1_cart*.svg,
cps2_cart*.svg), lit into their neutrals by examples/retro_neutrals.rs;
every other neutral regenerates byte for byte.
